<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Mantua</h1><p class="st-meta">1328 CE – 1708 CE · capital Mantua</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Gonzaga state of Mantua, whose court commissioned Mantegna, Giulio Romano and Monteverdi before war and plague ruined it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1328 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luigi-i-gonzaga">Luigi Gonzaga</a> overthrew the Bonacolsi lords of Mantua and became captain of the people. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> ruled as imperial vicars, became marquises in 1433 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gianfrancesco-i-gonzaga">Gianfrancesco Gonzaga</a> and dukes in 1530 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federico-ii-gonzaga-duke-of-mantua">Federico II</a>, who also acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-montferrat">Duchy of Montferrat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Mantua's court was among the most brilliant in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-mantegna">Andrea Mantegna</a> painted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camera-degli-sposi">Camera degli Sposi</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-iii-gonzaga">Ludovico III</a>; Isabella d'<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-este">Este</a> collected art; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giulio-romano">Giulio Romano</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-te">Palazzo Te</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federico-ii-gonzaga-duke-of-mantua">Federico II</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vincenzo-i-gonzaga">Vincenzo I</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/l-orfeo">Monteverdi's Orfeo</a> was staged in 1607. The duchy lived from farming, textiles and the condottiere service of its lords.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The main line died out in 1627, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-mantuan-succession">War of the Mantuan Succession</a> brought an imperial sack in 1630. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga-nevers">Gonzaga-Nevers</a> line ruled until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-carlo-gonzaga">Ferdinando Carlo</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and was deposed in 1708, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> annexed Mantua.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-mantua.jpg" alt="Duchy of Mantua" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Coat_of_arms_of_the_House_of_Gonzaga_(1575).svg: F l a n k e r derivative work: Amber and Black (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Duchy_of_Mantua_(1575%E2%80%931707).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1328 CE – 1708 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mantua</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ludovico III Gonzaga, Federico II Gonzaga, Vincenzo I Gonzaga</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Italian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marquisate of Mantua, Gonzaga Mantua, Mantua</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1518&amp;focus=duchy-of-mantua" aria-label="Duchy of Mantua on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4937 584 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Mantua lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5257 840L5201 840M5257 840L5201 840M5257 840L5229 694M5257 840L5381 747M5257 840L5257 840"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5201 840h0M5201 840h0M5229 694h0M5381 747h0M5257 840h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5257 840h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5257 840h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mantua. <a href="/atlas?